# =============================================================================
# Caddyfile.dashboard-block — the Metabase subdomain, appended onto the real Caddyfile
# =============================================================================
# Purpose:
#   `08-deploy-metabase.sh` builds the Metabase-enabled Caddy config by
#   concatenating `infra/Caddyfile` (unchanged, the one and only copy of the
#   app's own site block and its hardening headers) with this file, rather
#   than deploying a second, separately hand-maintained copy of the app's
#   site block that could drift from the real one and silently lose
#   hardening (ADR-13) the day either file changes without the other.
#   Sslip.io resolves any subdomain of a `<dashes>.sslip.io` name to the
#   same IP, so `dashboard.` needs no DNS record of its own; Caddy issues
#   that block its own certificate automatically, the same way it does for
#   the bare host name in `infra/Caddyfile`.
# Design:
#   A subdomain, not a path prefix, because Metabase does not support being
#   served under a non-root path without extra configuration this project
#   does not otherwise need. Deployed only after Metabase's first-run setup
#   succeeds (ADR-11: the reverse proxy must not reach Metabase before
#   then) — until `08-deploy-metabase.sh` runs, this file is never
#   appended to the live Caddyfile, so Metabase is unreachable through
#   Caddy by construction, not by a request-time check.
# Usage:
#   Concatenated onto `infra/Caddyfile` by `infra/scripts/
#   08-deploy-metabase.sh`; never deployed on its own, and not run directly
#   from this repository.
# =============================================================================

dashboard.{$HOST_NAME} {
	reverse_proxy metabase:3000
}
